lby-octavia-gcmouse: mouse movement through GameController, rewritten for Lullaby (replaces 0004 and 0005), 2026-10-23.

Origin: Elvin Hayatov's WineHQ merge request !11799 (bfa3c0fdc2da), via WineForge 0.6.0.7 (8051e02d); LGPL-2.1-or-later like
Wine, his notice kept in cocoa_gcmouse.m. What differs from his code:
 - no change to the build files: cocoa_gcmouse.m is included at the end of cocoa_event.m, and GameController is not
   linked (no Makefile.in line) but loaded when the first mouse is looked for;
 - a trackpad keeps the engine's own path "as is": AppKit's mouse-moved events are left out only while GameController
   delivered movement in the last 40 ms, so a pointer GameController does not report (the built-in trackpad is not a
   GCMouse here; one named "trackpad" is skipped) is not cut off or scaled;
 - the raw counts are scaled by the mouse's own resolution: LULLABY_GCMOUSE_SCALE=<number> sets it, anything else is
   automatic, 480 / counts-per-inch from the external mouse's HIDPointerResolution within 0.05 .. 2, and 0.3 (the
   calibration made on the owner's mouse) when no mouse reports a resolution; the fractions are carried over;
 - off unless the Mac driver key UseGCMouse or the environment variable LULLABY_GCMOUSE is on.

Requires: 0003-winemac-lullaby-vsync-and-present-feed.patch (the series order, no code dependency).
Verified on: built with the series on Dormison r7, 2026-10-23 (see patches/REGISTRY.md WIN... ENG-08); live check with a mouse and the trackpad by the owner.
Switch: LULLABY_GCMOUSE=0/1 (the game's settings), LULLABY_GCMOUSE_SCALE.
Test: patches/engine/lby-octavia-gcmouse/README.md (checks by hand: mouse speed, trackpad speed).

